description: Drive a csdd plan's autonomous loop — one Claude session per iteration, verified and approved by the runner, self-correcting on failure. Requires an approved, drift-free plan.
argument-hint: <plan-slug> [--yes]
allowed-tools: Bash(csdd plan run:*), Bash(csdd plan status:*), Bash(csdd plan unblock:*), Bash(npx @protonspy/csdd plan:*)
---

## Task

Drive the plan in `$ARGUMENTS` through `csdd plan run`.

Preflight first: `csdd plan status <slug>` must show the plan **approved** and
**drift-free**. Then:

- `csdd plan run <slug>` — the loop spawns one fresh session per iteration with
  `--dangerously-skip-permissions` (default cap 100, `--max-iterations`), runs the
  gates, and approves each phase only on green. Run it inside the hardened
  sandbox: the runner checks `csdd sandbox doctor` first, and when isolation is
  NOT verified it alerts and asks for confirmation — declining closes the run.
- `--yes` pre-accepts that alert (non-interactive runs); only pass it when the
  human has explicitly accepted running bypass-mode outside a verified sandbox.

The runner is only the loop and the verifier: it owns the phase approvals and the
journal, while the session controls the flow — it runs the csdd dev-cycle, owns
git (branch, `/csdd-commit`, the pre-push gate, the PR), and **makes and records
open decisions** (docs/stack.md Decided row / ADR, declared in the verdict's
`decisions`; the runner re-binds the approval automatically). Failures never park
a feat mid-run: each one becomes the next session's context, and the loop
self-corrects until the plan completes, a session halts, the stall guard trips
(`--stall`, default 10 sessions with no advancement), or the cap is hit.

## When the run ends without completing

`csdd plan status <slug>` prints each marker's **kind**. A marker records how the
run ENDED — the next `csdd plan run <slug>` clears it and retries automatically,
so the usual move is: read, fix if needed, run again. Never `rm` a marker under
`.csdd/` by hand.

- **`gate-failure`** — the run stalled or hit the cap on this step. Every
  attempt's output is in `.csdd/plan/<slug>/failures/<feat>/<step>.log`; **read
  that log first**. If something outside the loop's reach broke (tooling, env),
  fix it, then just re-run — the next run's first session is pointed at the log.
- **`halt`** — a session declared an impediment outside the workspace (missing
  credential, unreachable service, human-only access). Fix the impediment, then
  re-run. Do not `--force` past it without fixing anything.
- **`deviation`** (written by older csdd versions only) — an open decision the
  old runner parked on. The current loop retries it and lets the session decide
  and record; alternatively, fold the recorded proposal into the plan via the
  `prd` skill's Revise workflow and `csdd plan approve <slug>`.

Audit an autonomous run through `docs/plans/<slug>/log.md`: every step outcome,
failure, recorded decision, and contract re-bind is journaled there — ratify the
sessions' decisions by reading it after the run.
